Subject: [PATCH] sub: keep the ASS atlas when only positions or colors change

mp_ass_packer copied every libass bitmap into a fresh atlas on every frame
libass reported as changed. libass reports a change for a new color as
for new content, so a fade, a \move or a karaoke color step repacked (and
a GPU VO re-uploaded) the whole atlas although every bitmap was the one
already in it. Rendering the bench's anime-ass.mkv frame by frame with
this libass, 523 of the 779 changed frames (67%) draw exactly the previous
frame's bitmaps, and 94% of the bitmap bytes of all changed frames were in
the previous frame.

With --sub-ass-atlas-reuse (default yes), sd_ass' packer holds the image
list it packed last with ass_frame_ref (libass 0006), so none of its
bitmaps can be freed and their memory taken by a bitmap of the next frame:
equal pointer, size and stride then mean equal pixels. A frame whose parts
are, in order, exactly those bitmaps keeps the atlas: each part keeps its
place in it and only its screen position and color change. The result
carries the atlas' new atlas_id field (sub_bitmaps), equal across such
frames, which tells a VO that caches the atlas on the GPU that it can draw
the new frame from the uploaded copy; change_id still changes, so every
other consumer behaves as before. osd_ahead's dedup carries atlas_id over
with the atlas it adopts. Only mask atlases from a single list (sd_ass)
are reused; the BGRA path bakes the colors into the atlas.

A new atlas is still needed for the other frames, and consumers hold the
previous ones (osd_ahead slots, an upload in flight), so every such frame
allocated afresh: on Android a scudo secondary allocation, which means an
mmap, a page fault per page during the copy, and a munmap when the last
consumer lets go. --sub-ass-atlas-pool keeps that many earlier atlases
and reuses one nobody references any more. It defaults to 4 on Android
and to 0 elsewhere: on an iPhone the spares saved no CPU and held 7 MB.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index be1cf56..b82d6cc 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -2674,6 +2674,23 @@ Subtitles
 
     Default: 0.
 
+``--sub-ass-atlas-reuse=<yes|no>``
+    When a libass frame draws exactly the bitmaps of the previous frame, only
+    at other positions or in other colors (a fade, a ``\move``, a karaoke
+    color step), keep the previous frame's packed atlas instead of copying
+    every bitmap into a new one. VOs that cache the atlas on the GPU
+    (``vo_mediacodec``) then skip its upload as well. The output is the same.
+
+    Default: yes.
+
+``--sub-ass-atlas-pool=<0-8>``
+    How many earlier subtitle atlases to keep, so that a new atlas can reuse
+    one a VO has finished with instead of allocating (and page-faulting) a
+    fresh one. Spares are at most the size the atlas has grown to. 0
+    allocates every atlas anew.
+
+    Default: 4 on Android, 0 elsewhere.
+
 ``--sub-ass-styles=<filename>``
     Load all SSA/ASS styles found in the specified file and use them for
     rendering text subtitles. The syntax of the file is exactly like the ``[V4
